      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single dose also normally doesn't exceed 1,000 queryable mg. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, which can be life-threatening. The dose may be a typo. For example, 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg twice daily would be within range.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order is intended or authorized.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. Once I have a corrected dose, or the prescriber confirms this one is deliberate, I can enter it. I can also enter it if you tell me the order is coming from a prescriber."
      }
